1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,030
Tim: Good morning.

2
00:00:03,030 --> 00:00:09,090
You're through to the tourist information office, Tim speaking. How can I help you?

3
00:00:09,090 --> 00:00:14,570
Jean: Oh hello. Could you give me some information about next month's festival, please?

4
00:00:14,570 --> 00:00:19,000
My family and I will be staying in the town that week.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,740
Tim: Of course. Well it starts with a concert on the afternoon of the 17th.

6
00:00:23,740 --> 00:00:25,660
Jean: Oh I heard about that

7
00:00:25,660 --> 00:00:29,110
The orchestra and singers come from the USA, don't they?

8
00:00:29,110 --> 00:00:33,650
Tim: They're from Canada. They're very popular over there.

9
00:00:33,650 --> 00:00:39,700
They're going to perform a number of well-known pieces that will appeal to children as well as adults.

10
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:43,700
Jean: That sounds good. My whole family are interested in music.

11
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:45,840
Tim: The next day, the 18th

12
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:50,770
there's a performance by a ballet company called Eustatis.

13
00:00:50,770 --> 00:00:51,740
Jean: Sorry?

14
00:00:51,740 --> 00:00:59,420
Tim: The name is spelt E-U-S-T-A-T-I-S.

15
00:00:59,420 --> 00:01:03,310
They appeared in last year's festival, and went down very well.

16
00:01:03,310 --> 00:01:07,060
Again, their programme is designed for all ages.

17
00:01:07,060 --> 00:01:09,850
Jean: Good. I expect we'll go to that.

18
00:01:09,850 --> 00:01:15,270
I hope there's going to be a play during the festival, a comedy, ideally.

19
00:01:15,270 --> 00:01:16,630
Tim: You're in luck!

20
00:01:16,630 --> 00:01:23,600
On the 19th and 20th a local amateur group are performing one written by a member of the group.

21
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:28,390
It's called Jemima. That will be on in the town hall.

22
00:01:28,390 --> 00:01:31,040
They've already performed it two or three times.

23
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:36,330
I haven't seen it myself, but the review in the local paper was very good.

24
00:01:36,330 --> 00:01:39,040
Jean: And is it suitable for children?

25
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:43,500
Tim: Yes, in fact it's aimed more at children than at adults

26
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:46,730
so both performances are in the afternoon.

27
00:01:46,730 --> 00:01:51,470
Jean: And what about dance? Will there be any performances?

28
00:01:51,470 --> 00:01:54,870
Tim: Yes, also on the 20th, but in the evening.

29
00:01:54,870 --> 00:01:58,620
A professional company is putting on a show of modern pieces

30
00:01:58,620 --> 00:02:02,270
with electronic music by young composers.

31
00:02:02,270 --> 00:02:03,030
Jean: Uh-huh.

32
00:02:03,030 --> 00:02:06,237
Tim: The show is about how people communicate,

33
00:02:06,237 --> 00:02:12,250
or fail to communicate, with each other, so it's got the rather strange name, Chat.

34
00:02:12,250 --> 00:02:18,040
Jean: I suppose that's because that's something we do both face to face and online.

35
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:20,890
Tim: That's right.

36
00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:26,110
Tim: Now there are also some workshops and other activities.

37
00:02:26,110 --> 00:02:29,600
They'll all take place at least once every day

38
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:32,630
so everyone who wants to take part will have a chance.

39
00:02:32,630 --> 00:02:36,540
Jean: Good. We're particularly interested in cookery

40
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:40,100
you don't happen to have a cookery workshop, do you?

41
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:47,135
Tim: We certainly do. It's going to focus on how to make food part of a healthy lifestyle,

42
00:02:47,135 --> 00:02:54,170
and it'll show that even sweet things like cakes can contain much less sugar than they usually do.

43
00:02:54,170 --> 00:02:59,680
Jean: That might be worth going to. We're trying to encourage our children to cook.

44
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:02,680
Tim: Another workshop is just for children

45
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:07,690
and that's on creating posters to reflect the history of the town.

46
00:03:07,690 --> 00:03:11,820
The aim is to make children aware of how both the town

47
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:16,000
and people's lives have changed over the centuries.

48
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,540
The results will be exhibited in the community centre.

49
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:25,720
Then the other workshop is in toy-making, and that's for adults only.

50
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:27,490
Jean: Oh, why's that?

51
00:03:27,490 --> 00:03:32,800
Tim: Because it involves carpentry - participants will be making toys out of wood,

52
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:38,110
so there will be a lot of sharp chisels and other tools around.

53
00:03:38,110 --> 00:03:41,480
Jean: It makes sense to keep children away from it.

54
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:46,700
Tim: Exactly. Now let me tell you about some of the outdoor activities.

55
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:49,460
There will be supervised wild swimming...

56
00:03:49,460 --> 00:03:52,300
Jean: Wild swimming? What's that?

57
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:57,350
Tim: It just means swimming in natural waters, rather than a swimming pool.

58
00:03:57,350 --> 00:04:00,450
Jean: Oh OK. In a lake, for instance.

59
00:04:00,450 --> 00:04:04,040
Tim: Yes, there's a beautiful one just outside the town

60
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:06,740
and that will be the venue for the swimming.

61
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:11,520
There will be lifeguards on duty, so it's suitable for all ages.

62
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:17,000
And finally, there will be a walk in some nearby woods every day.

63
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:20,650
The leader is an expert on insects.

64
00:04:20,650 --> 00:04:22,900
He'll show some that live in the woods

65
00:04:22,900 --> 00:04:25,700
and how important they are for the environment.

66
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:30,770
So there are going to be all sorts of different things to do during the festival.

67
00:04:30,770 --> 00:04:32,520
Jean: There certainly are.

68
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:37,300
Tim: If you'd like to read about how the preparations for the festival are going,

69
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:39,530
the festival organizer is keeping a blog.

70
00:04:39,530 --> 00:04:44,560
Just search online for the festival website, and you'll find it.

71
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:48,040
Jean: Well, thank you very much for all the information.

72
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,700
Tim: You're welcome. Goodbye.

73
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:52,000
Jean: Goodbye.
